# 27b. Agent Instance Subdomains (wildcard, on-demand TLS)
# Dynamic per-instance routes are prepended via Caddy admin API; this
# wildcard MUST be the last route so specific-host routes win.
#
# TLS strategy:
#   * In production (TLS_MODE empty → Let's Encrypt) we use ON-DEMAND TLS.
#     Wildcard certs need DNS-01, which we don't ship a plugin for. Instead,
#     each per-user subdomain (e.g. hermes-a3f8c2.agents.<domain>) gets its
#     own per-name LE cert at first visit via HTTP-01. agent-manager exposes
#     /api/tls/ask which Caddy queries before issuing — only registered
#     instance hostnames are allowed, blocking cert-flood DoS.
#   * In dev (TLS_MODE=internal → tls_config = "tls internal") the import
#     overrides on_demand and Caddy issues from its internal CA, no LE
#     dependency.
*.{$AGENTS_DOMAIN} {
    tls {
        on_demand
    }
    import tls_config
    import security_headers

    # SECURITY (C1 layer-1, PR #84 adversarial review): the per-instance agent
    # subdomains serve a live shell (coding-agent web terminal) and per-user
    # UIs — they MUST be Authentik-gated exactly like the base {$AGENTS_DOMAIN}
    # site. Without this forward_auth an unauthenticated request that falls
    # through to this wildcard (e.g. a not-yet-registered / just-lost dynamic
    # route) reached agent-manager — and, for the admin-API dynamic routes,
    # the agent container — with NO auth. The dynamically-registered
    # specific-host routes now ALSO inject their own forward_auth handler
    # (caddy_client.register_route), and the container enforces owner identity
    # itself (defence-in-depth).
    @agents_wild_protected {
        not path /outpost.goauthentik.io/*
        not path /branding/*
        not path /healthz
        not method OPTIONS
    }
    forward_auth @agents_wild_protected authentik-server:9000 {
        import authentik_upstream_config
    }

    handle /outpost.goauthentik.io/* {
        reverse_proxy authentik-server:9000
    }

    # C1 bypass fix — "came through Caddy" is anchored by a SOURCE-IP check at
    # agent-manager (proxy.py), not an injected header (see the removed
    # (manager_proxy_proof) snippet note above). agent-manager 403s any request
    # whose peer IP isn't Caddy's.
    reverse_proxy agent-manager:5000
}

# 27c. Personal MCP Manager UI (Profile: mcp) [EXPERIMENTAL] (#36)
# Per-user MCP-proxy provisioning + encrypted credential vault. SSO-gated via
