# 27d. Personal MCP per-user proxy subdomains (wildcard) (#36)
# Each provisioned per-user MCP proxy gets an opaque-token subdomain
# ({mcp_id}-{token}.{$MCP_DOMAIN}) registered as a SPECIFIC-HOST route via the
# Caddy admin API by mcp-manager's caddy_client at provision time (those routes
# reverse-proxy straight to the per-user proxy container, which authenticates
# the agent->proxy call with its own bearer token; they are removed at stop and
# reconciled on boot). Those admin-API routes are host-specific and `terminal`,
# so they always win over this static catch-all.
#
# SECURITY (commit-review CRITICAL #1): this static wildcard MUST NOT expose the
# MCP MANAGER (mcp-manager:5000 — credential vault + UI + internal endpoints).
# The manager is reachable ONLY via the SSO-gated exact-host {$MCP_DOMAIN} block
# above. Any *.{$MCP_DOMAIN} host that does NOT match a registered per-proxy
# admin-API route is unknown and is refused here (404) — it must never fall
# through to the manager unauthenticated. TLS for the per-proxy subdomains is
# automated by the per-route internal-CA tls policy the admin API installs
# (mirrors agent-manager's caddy_client), so no blanket on_demand is needed.
*.{$MCP_DOMAIN} {
    import tls_config
    respond "Not found" 404
}

